/*! \mainpage GNU Radio CaribouLite receive source

The caribouLiteSource block receives through the native CaribouLite C++ API.
It outputs complex float IQ and optional byte metadata. Its channel parameter
selects S1G (0) or HiF (1); other parameters select AGC, gain, bandwidth, sample
rate, frequency, metadata and PMOD state. Construction initializes the board
and starts receiving. No native transmit sink is implemented.

Python/GRC bindings, when enabled and installed, use the namespace
`from gnuradio import caribouLite`. See the module README for source-build
instructions, example requirements and the outstanding end-to-end validation.
*/
